uve</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Costa</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Sacchini</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Maltoni</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Robertson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Rotmensz</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Boyle</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prevention of breast cancer with tamoxifen: preliminary findings from the Italian randomised trial among hysterectomised women</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1998</year><volume>352</volume><fpage>93</fpage><lpage>97</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Lancet||352|93||bib31|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9672273</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wagner</surname><given-names>TMU</given-names></name><name><surname>M&#x000f6;slinger</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Muhr</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Langbauer</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Hirtenlehner</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Concin</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Doeller</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Haid</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lang</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Mayer</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Roff</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Kubista</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Amirimani</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Helbich</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Becherer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Scheiner</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Breiteneder</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Borg</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Devilee</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Oefner</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Zielinski</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>BRCA1-related breast cancer in Austrian breast and ovarian cancer families: specific BRCA1 mutations and pathological characteristics</article-title><source>Int J Cancer</source><year>1998</year><volume>77</volume><fpage>354</fpage><lpage>360</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Int J Cancer||77|354||bib32|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9663595</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><app-group><app id="app1"><title>APPENDIX 1</title><sec><title>Approximate confidence interval for the two-stage method</title><p>The square of the standard error of <italic>R</italic> is the variance of <italic>R</italic>, denoted <italic>V(R)</italic>.</p><p><disp-formula id="equ2"><!-- in formula template--><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="86-6600064e2.jpg"/></disp-formula></p><p>where <italic>C</italic> represents the covariance. Noting that <italic>V(p)</italic> &#x0003d;<italic>V(1-p)</italic> and assuming <italic>R</italic><sub>&#x0002b;</sub>, R<sub>&#x02212;</sub> and <italic>p</italic> are independent, the above can be estimated as</p><p><disp-formula id="equ3"><!-- in formula template--><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="86-6600064e3.jpg"/></disp-formula></p><p>Using the delta method we can approximate the standard error of the logarithm of the relative risk <italic>R</italic> as</p><p><disp-formula id="equ4"><!-- in formula template--><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="86-6600064e4.jpg"/></disp-formula></p><p>We then calculate the confidence interval on the log relative risk and retransform to the linear scale in the usual way.</p></sec></app></app-group></back></article>